    "narrative": "As we enter the home stretch of September, our offensive strategy for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on maximizing run production against high-xERA arms, with **Josh Naylor** (75.33) and **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) leading the charge as our premier starts. **Josh Naylor** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Jose Quintana, whose 5.92 xERA combined with a significant park factor boost puts him in a prime position to anchor the middle of our order. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** is locked into a high-upside spot against Nick Lodolo; his elite BvP history (+8%) and advantageous platoon split make him an essential play, despite the inherent risk of Lodolo\u2019s stuff. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) and **Mickey Moniak** (71.55) also warrant high-leverage starts, with the latter benefiting from a massive +14% platoon adjustment and a matchup against a pitcher with a slow delivery, providing a sneaky boost to his stolen base potential.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today is **Austin Riley**, who posted a solid 57.09 but fell just short of displacing our lower-tier starters. While **Austin Riley** offers stability, the optimizer preferred the high-ceiling platoon edges offered by **Cole Young** and **Mickey Moniak**, whose specific matchups provided the incremental score necessary to stay above the 60.0 threshold. We must maintain vigilance regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while we have assumed optimal placements for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Moises Ballesteros**, and **Isaac Paredes**, any shifts in the batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to preserve our limited game caps. Furthermore, while **Corbin Carroll** holds a respectable 54.06, he faces an elite arm in Cam Schlittler (2.88 xERA), meaning he remains a marginal start strictly for his speed tool, as the pitching matchup significantly caps his overall output. Proceed with caution on **Jose Caballero** as well; while his stolen base floor is valuable, his negative platoon adjustment against Brandon Pfaadt suggests we should temper expectations.",
